# Generated graphify output — tracked as deliverables (see graphify-out/.gitignore
# and CLAUDE.md § graphify) but NOT prettier-owned. graph.html is emitted compact
# by `graphify update`; letting prettier reformat it churns it 306 -> ~179k lines
# and the salt-autofix bot (.github/workflows/autofix.yml) then force-pushes that
# expansion onto every PR. Excluding the dir stops both the reformat and the
# `pnpm format:check` (CI Format check) drift on these files.
graphify-out/

# pnpm's lockfile — generated, and owned by the package manager's own writer.
# It entered prettier's scope when `format`'s glob widened to `.yaml` (#1168).
# Reformatting it puts every `pnpm install` in a fight with `pnpm format`: pnpm
# rewrites the file in its own style, `format:check` then reds CI, and the
# autofix bot pushes the reflow back. Nobody reads it by hand, so there is
# nothing to gain on the other side of that trade.
pnpm-lock.yaml
